<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John II, Duke of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1341–<a href="/years/1397">1397</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John II was a Wittelsbach Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> who ruled jointly with his brothers Stephen III and Frederick until the partition of 1392 gave him the lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>, creating the Duchy of Bavaria-Munich. After his death in 1397 his sons Ernest and William III ruled jointly. His line, based in Munich, outlasted the rival Bavarian branches and reunited the country under Albert IV in 1505.</p></div>
